e it goes below a certain point the  heat kicks in again and then it brings  it up a certain point and so ovens kind  of waver between 10 degrees 5 degrees it  depends on your oven so I just pulled  these amazing chocolate chip cookies out  of the oven and I'm going to let them  rest here for about 10 minutes before I  take them off and put them on the  cooling tray I think we should try some  of the warm cookies oh my gosh is your  cookie like this there's like gooey milk  chocolate and gooey dark chocolate  inside and so let's go ahead and  mmm  what am I looking for  you can see visually  your cookies are golden brown  pale in the center  but they're totally cooked through in  the center if you pull them out too  early you're going to end up with this  little pocket of raw dough it won't be  the end of the world but ideally you  want the cookie to be baked all the way  through for me the perfect chocolate  chip cookie is kind of balanced with a  lot of chocolate flavor it's got a  crispy Edge it's got a tender melt in  your mouth center it's got big pieces of  chocolate all throughout there's also a  little hint of molasses it's from the  brown sugar and a little caramel from  the milk chocolate  and then there's just a little bit of  salt we put in that kosher salt into the  recipe and you can actually taste a  little hint of salt it's not salty by  any means but it's enough salt to really  draw out the flavors of the butter the  vanilla and all of the chocolate  they are definitely best eaten day of  that you bake them but if you store them  they should last about two more days in  an airtight container so now you've  become a star cookie Baker if you really  want to improve your cookie baking  there's one simple trick just keep  making cookies and who's going to  complain about that making cookies over  and over again you will get so much  practice and you will learn how every  single little adjustment you make  changes the result of the cookie and  you'll be 